@@ -112,2 +112,3 @@
 decision/identity-by-instance · Identity by instance, never by location — Every hook, MCP call and CLI verb finds its instance through `VIOLA_NAME` or an explicit `ViolaName` argument, never through the working directory; instances are identified by `ViolaName`, endpoints by its short hash, and there are no database keys. · why: Two sessions in one folder never share records; identity is by instance, never by location (R5).
+decision/identity-floor-ledger-row · Identity-floor ledger row and its readings — The identity-floor relied ledger row passes when every CLAUDE name the CLI adds to a SessionStart hook is an identity-floor name or a known non-identity name, and fails on an unknown name or an unread or off-shape env-names file; kept names are dropped before the check.
 decision/installed-plugin-mcp-only · Installed plugin carries MCP only — viola plugin install is optional, for the MCP verbs in an unwrapped driver; the installed plugin carries only .mcp.json and no hooks, its command the absolute path of the installing exe. · why: So a wrapped session that also has it installed never runs two hook processes for one event.
@@ -170,3 +171,3 @@
 decision/pty-error-hand-written · Hand-written PTY error type — The PTY crate's error has a hand-written Display and Error with fixed messages, keeping the portable-pty anyhow error only as a boxed source. · why: The seam's normal dependencies are exactly portable-pty, tracing and libc; an exception to the thiserror rule.
-decision/r8-identity-floor · R8 parent-identity floor — The measured CLAUDE* parent-identity environment names are stripped from the child even when the persistent environment defines them; every other CLAUDE* name follows the prefix rule.
+decision/r8-identity-floor · R8 parent-identity floor — The identity-floor CLAUDE* parent-identity environment names are stripped from the child even when the persistent environment defines them; every other CLAUDE* name follows the prefix rule.
 decision/reader-counts-skipped-lines · Event reader counts what it skips — The event reader counts unknown kinds, unknown fields and torn lines per read and does not log the counts.
@@ -621,2 +622,3 @@
 contract/ledger-stamps/content · ledger stamps envelope · content — Per CLI version, the envelope holds each ledger row's `pass` or `fail`, `absent` also for browser-tools-prompt, or for trust-record the trust writer's word when no record was written, and the probe's measured values, of which `run` reads none.
+contract/ledger-stamps/env-probe · ledger stamps envelope · measured.env_probe — Holds read, added, unknown, other_count and unshaped from the identity-floor probe, names only, with every kept name removed.
 contract/ledger-stamps/first-screen · ledger stamps envelope · measured.first_screen — For each of the six interactive verify runs, one closed word naming its first settled screen: trust, imports, browser-tools, box, none or exited; no screen text.
@@ -712,3 +714,2 @@
 decision/hook-missing-instance-dir-exits-silently · Hook with a missing instance folder exits 0 silently — A hook whose VIOLA_DIR names an instance folder that does not exist fails the canonical-directory step, exits 0 and writes nothing: no role file, no stdin read, no frame and no event line. · why: Claude Code runs the plugin's hooks in sessions viola does not wrap; the hook fail-open contract and its no-instance-directory test rely on it.
-decision/identity-floor-eleven-names · Identity floor of eleven names — The identity floor is CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_BRIDGE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT, CLAUDE_CODE_EXECPATH, CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_SOCKET, CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_TOKEN, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ATTENDED, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_EFFORT and CLAUDE_PID. · why: The plugin and project names a hook sees are not identity names, and the prefix rule already removes them when inherited.
 decision/linked-e2e-home-base-strict · Linked e2e-home base must be a private real directory — A linked e2e-home base must have an absolute target, created with mode 0700 when gone and never chmodded after, and is accepted only when it reads as a real directory with no group or other bit; anything else refuses the start with a fixed message naming no path.
@@ -726,5 +727,5 @@
 decision/plugin-carries-no-hooks · Installed plugin carries no hooks — The plugin `viola plugin install` adds registers the MCP server `viola` in its `.mcp.json` and carries no hooks.
-decision/plugin-env-vars-unused · Plugin-provided environment variables unused — viola never uses CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT or CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA to locate its binary, and reads none of those or CLAUDE_ENV_FILE and CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR.
+decision/plugin-env-vars-unused · Plugin-provided environment variables unused — viola never uses CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT or CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA to locate its binary and reads no value of those, CLAUDE_ENV_FILE or CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR; the four are known non-identity hook names, read by name only by the identity-floor ledger check.
 decision/plugin-install-rewrites-marketplace-whole · Plugin install rewrites the marketplace tree whole — The plugin marketplace tree is rewritten whole on every plugin install, any other entry there is left as found, and viola never reads the tree back. · why: A rerun re-points the MCP server at the current exe and home, the rerun test expects the same tree, and only its folders need the strict-modes check.
-decision/probe-capture-arms-inert · Probe capture arms are inert — The hidden hook `--capture` arm takes an absolute, existing directory only, reads no `VIOLA_*` variable, starts no observability, opens no channel, and always exits 0 with empty stderr.
+decision/probe-capture-arms-inert · Probe capture arms are inert — The hidden hook `--capture` arm takes an absolute, existing directory only, reads no `VIOLA_*` variable and no environment value, starts no observability, opens no channel, and always exits 0 with empty stderr.
 decision/process-logs-hold-codes-only · Home-level process logs hold codes only — Home-level per-role process logs carry codes only, one line per write; content-bearing detail stays in the instance detail files.
@@ -805,2 +806,3 @@
 contract/harness-environment/agent-run-keep-homes · test harness environment · AGENT_RUN_KEEP_HOMES — The value 1 keeps the test and session homes for the CI gates.
+contract/hook-capture-arm/env-names-file · viola hook --capture arm · env-names file — On SessionStart alone the capture arm also writes Env.<k>.json owner-only beside the payload, holding the CLAUDE names of its own process with every other name only counted; no value is ever read or written.
 contract/hook-capture-arm/exit · viola hook --capture arm · exit status — Always exit 0 with empty stderr; no VIOLA_* variable read, no diagnostics started, no channel opened.
